  "strategy": "1. Approach and rationale\nThe problem may be addressed by combining a time-frequency analysis inclination with a constrained local optimization. Representing the step function h as a high-resolution discretization allows for more precise boundary exploration. By examining the integral of h(x)(1-h(x+k)) as a correlation function across all shifts, we can view this as a discrete convolution problem. The repair_vector function ensures integral constraints by iteratively relocating mass to meet the required sum. Using This approach improves upon previous methods by introducing clearer local exploitation phases with dynamic repair prioritization and a more structured explorative phase with controlled noise addition.\n\n2. Mathematical specification\n   -Variable bounds: h[i] \u2208 [0,1]\u2200i\n   -Constraint: \u03a3h[i] = n_points/2 (exactly)\n   -Objective: E = max_k [np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full') * dx]\n   -Repair: reallocates mass for constraint satisfaction while bounding adjustments to local regions to minimize perturbation.\n\n3. Implementation procedure\n   - Validate the initial solution if available\n   - Implement a repair mechanism that independently fulfills integral constraints like mass locality hypothesis\n   - Define separate optimization strategies for refinement and district exploration\n   - Monitor time during MCMC sampling\n   - Strictly enforce constraint satisfaction via multiple repair attempts or fallback\n\n4. Search choices\n   - Primary: multiple repair strategies for constraint satisfaction\n   - Secondary: incremental refinement and volumetric perturbation\n   - Metrics: explore/ exploit balance, cache reuse efficiency\n   - Fallback: geometric projection fallback when repair fails\n\n5. Computebudget and robustness\n   -Dominant cost: correlation computation (O(n_points^2))\n   -Fallback fallthrough: priority strategy with repair attempt count\n   -Batch-sequential repair: dynamic scaling ensures endurance\n\n6. Validation and return contract\n   - Meticulously repair every candidate to satisfy constraints\n   - Execute objective evaluation with numpy.corralation.full mode\n   - Return with strict type checking and time monitoring",
